Nemotron 3.5 Lightning speculative decoding (PR #36186 + the two DFlash2
prerequisites #35371/#35496) patch-application step for
container-build/Dockerfile.sglang-nightly.

Adds one COPY+RUN step that applies sglang-nemotron35-spec-pr36186.patch to the
sglang Python source AFTER the SM121 sgl-kernel patches but BEFORE
`uv pip install ./python`, so the installed package picks up the new speculative
paths. Same pattern as dockerfile-qwen36-mixed-nvfp4.patch / dockerfile-qwen4exp.patch.

Apply to: container-build/Dockerfile.sglang-nightly AFTER dockerfile-sm121.patch
has been applied. Application is gated by build_sm121_image.sh on the recipe
variable APPLY_NEMOTRON35_SPEC_PR36186=1 (set in sglang-0.5.18-sm121.recipe;
remove the variable / set 0 once the pinned SGLANG_REF already contains the
merge commit 41e7612dee — re-applying merged code fails the in-container
dry-run and aborts the build, which is the intended loud failure).

STACKABLE: like dockerfile-qwen36-mixed-nvfp4.patch and dockerfile-qwen4exp.patch
this hunk uses ONLY trailing context (the `# Install sglang package` comment
block) with no leading context, so it inserts immediately before that comment
regardless of whether another model patch (dsv4, qwen36, qwen4exp) already
inserted its COPY+RUN block there first. build_sm121_image.sh applies this as
step 2i, after 2c (dsv4), 2f (qwen36) and 2h (qwen4exp), so on a recipe with
several of them enabled this block ends up last, directly before
`# Install sglang`. Works standalone too.

SCOPE NOTE: this build step covers the three speculative decoders (MTP / DFlash /
DSpark) for nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Lightning-30B-A3B-NVFP4. Serving that
TARGET without speculation needs none of it — v0.5.18 already carries the
mixed-NVFP4 support (merged PR #27906) the checkpoint requires.

--- a/container-build/Dockerfile.sglang-nightly
+++ b/container-build/Dockerfile.sglang-nightly
@@ -293,3 +293,24 @@
+# Nemotron 3.5 Lightning speculative decoding (upstream PR #36186, MERGED
+# 2026-08-25, three days AFTER the v0.5.18 tag — plus its two DFlash2
+# prerequisites #35371 and #35496, without which #36186 does not apply to
+# v0.5.18 at all). 16 files: the NemotronH aux-hidden-state capture hook that
+# DFLASH/DSPARK hard-require, the Nemotron-3.5 DFlash/DSpark draft layouts
+# (draft-owned embeddings, packed projections, attention sinks, Markov bonus
+# anchor), ModelOpt W4A16 NVFP4 for the two published draft checkpoints, and the
+# Nemotron-H target/draft attention-backend resolver. Applied to the sglang
+# Python source before pip install so the installed dist-packages picks up the
+# changes. This COPY+RUN step only exists in builds whose recipe sets
+# APPLY_NEMOTRON35_SPEC_PR36186=1 (the dockerfile patch adding this step is
+# gated by build_sm121_image.sh).
+COPY patches/sglang-nemotron35-spec-pr36186.patch /tmp/sglang-nemotron35-spec-pr36186.patch
+RUN set -e; cd /data/sglang && \
+    echo "=== Applying sglang-nemotron35-spec-pr36186.patch (PR #36186 + #35371 + #35496) ===" && \
+    patch --dry-run -p1 < /tmp/sglang-nemotron35-spec-pr36186.patch && \
+    patch -p1 < /tmp/sglang-nemotron35-spec-pr36186.patch && \
+    grep -q 'def set_dflash_layers_to_capture' python/sglang/srt/models/nemotron_h.py && \
+    grep -q 'def is_nemotron_35_draft_config' python/sglang/srt/speculative/dflash_utils.py && \
+    echo 'Nemotron 3.5 spec PR #36186 patch applied successfully'
+
 # Install sglang package (no deps, no build isolation since base has torch).
 # Moved here from its original early-stage location so the installed
 # dist-packages picks up the patched nvfp4_blockwise_moe.cuh above.
